 "what_landed": "Every decaying-stack ramp opens the fight EMPTY. The walker seeded both the build's item ramp and a kit ramp with one stack live at t=0, so the first swing was rated as though an attack had already landed.",
 "why": [
  "The source is the item's own sentence: Guinsoo's Rageblade reads \"Basic attacks GRANT 8% bonus attack speed for 3 seconds, stacking up to 4 times\". The attack grants the stack, so the attack that lands one cannot be rated by it, because its own rate was fixed before it landed. Each swing is rated by the swings strictly before it.",
  "Two tests in tests/test_interp_charged_strike.py already SAID this and asserted the opposite, which is the strongest evidence the seed was a defect rather than a modelling choice. One is docstringed \"Later intervals are shorter than the first, which carries no bonus\" and then asserted the first interval was shorter than the bare rate. The other is docstringed \"each stack expires before the next hit, so one stays live\", which is self-contradictory: if each expires, none stays live. Both now assert what their docstrings always described, 1.0s then 1/1.08 for the first, and a flat 5.0s for the second.",
  "The stack is also recorded at the instant the attack HAPPENED rather than at the one it buys, so its three-second life is measured from the right end.",
  "Measured. A Rageblade-only seven-second fight goes from 9 scheduled autos and 2 phantom hits to 8 and 1, so its on-hit applications go 11 -> 9. The item sweep moves for Guinsoo's Rageblade alone: Ziggs 12s 2812.83 -> 2716.74 and 30s 5788.33 -> 5596.14. Jinx with no items, whose only ramp is her kit's, buys 4 autos per rotation where a seeded ramp claimed 5.",
  "The moved population is exactly the ramps: 2 item_sweep leaves, all of them Rageblade's, and 36 registered_champion_fights leaves across Jax and Jinx, the two champions on the kit ramp. One coupled roster holds a ramp and it is cleaver_bloodsong, whose swing stream shortened and cascaded through its event ledger."
 ],
 "qualifying_population": {
  "enumerated_before_first_src_edit": false,
  "rule": "Rageblade is the only item declaring a decaying-stack ramp and Jax and Jinx are the only kits declaring one, so the population is those three holders and the one coupled roster that holds any of them."
 },
